WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:07.882
[opening theme music playing]

01:46.731 --> 01:48.274
[music fades]

01:49.109 --> 01:56.116
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

01:59.744 --> 02:00.995
[solemn music playing]

02:02.872 --> 02:04.290
[Chae-ok] Since I was young,

02:06.000 --> 02:08.128
I dreamed of an ordinary life.

02:10.630 --> 02:14.342
I dreamed of the possible conversations
during family dinners,

02:14.425 --> 02:17.595
and everyone sharing stories
about how their day went.

02:20.348 --> 02:21.808
And I dreamed about a future

02:23.518 --> 02:24.769
with the person I love.

02:25.854 --> 02:27.021
It's all I ever wanted.

02:36.865 --> 02:38.658
I wished that I could…

02:41.494 --> 02:42.871
live the kind of life

02:44.455 --> 02:46.666
everyone else dreams of.

02:48.710 --> 02:49.669
[gunshot echoes]

02:59.095 --> 03:01.306
[Maeda] How foolish to think
you could have such a dream.

03:01.389 --> 03:02.849
[gasping]

03:07.645 --> 03:10.523
To think a Joseon woman would dare
to have any aspirations

03:10.607 --> 03:12.025
is completely senile.

03:12.108 --> 03:13.985
To do so will only bring suffering.

03:16.905 --> 03:18.198
Why are you holding me hostage?

03:20.408 --> 03:22.243
Well, because I was very curious

03:23.161 --> 03:25.747
to finally meet
Seishin's daughter in person.

03:27.665 --> 03:32.212
Now that I have seen you up close…
it's apparent you are indeed related.

03:32.295 --> 03:33.296
You have her eyes.

03:35.798 --> 03:37.592
How do you know who my mother is?

03:38.843 --> 03:41.179
That is no concern of yours, I'm afraid.

03:41.971 --> 03:45.850
But it's funny how the world works
in mysterious ways, don't you think?

03:45.934 --> 03:48.186
It was only a matter of time
before we met.

03:49.896 --> 03:51.522
In the end, we are all

03:51.606 --> 03:54.734
linked together, Seishin, you, and myself.

03:56.319 --> 03:57.862
Fate has bound us in the end.

04:02.242 --> 04:04.869
[Mr. Gu] Beom-o has told me
he knows where Yoon Chae-ok was taken.

04:06.246 --> 04:07.455
[Mrs. Nawol] You trust him?

04:07.538 --> 04:09.999
Do you seriously believe
what he says at all?

04:10.083 --> 04:11.459
How do we know he saw her?

04:11.542 --> 04:12.877
Oh, but I'm sure of it!

04:13.711 --> 04:15.964
I… I just saw her with my own two eyes.

04:16.047 --> 04:18.424
You have no credibility,
do you understand?

04:18.508 --> 04:21.219
How could you betray
the hand that feeds you, huh?

04:21.302 --> 04:23.429
[Mr. Gu] He's already heard
those words from me.

04:23.513 --> 04:25.765
You were living on the streets, kid.

04:25.848 --> 04:28.393
Master Jang gave you a home.
You are so ungrateful.

04:28.476 --> 04:30.144
I already made that point too.

04:30.228 --> 04:32.897
Lady Maeda said Master Jang
wouldn't be harmed at all.

04:32.981 --> 04:35.650
She told me he'd be safe
if I reported the sleuth woman to her.

04:35.733 --> 04:38.403
She said it would help Master Jang.
I'm really sorry.

04:40.196 --> 04:42.490
[Mrs. Nawol] My goodness,
you thick-headed idiot.

04:42.573 --> 04:44.742
You actually believed that woman? Huh?

04:46.536 --> 04:47.662
[Mrs. Nawol sighs]

04:56.212 --> 04:59.507
Where is she?
Tell me where they are keeping Chae-ok.

05:00.717 --> 05:02.010
[ominous music playing]

05:06.931 --> 05:08.099
Where is the prisoner?

05:08.182 --> 05:10.685
Lady Maeda just sent us
a Josenjing woman for you to see.

05:13.896 --> 05:14.897
[door clunks open]

05:25.700 --> 05:26.701
[Chae-ok grunting]

05:33.958 --> 05:34.917
[pained groaning]

05:45.261 --> 05:46.137
[chuckles softly]

05:48.222 --> 05:49.974
[snarls]

05:51.934 --> 05:53.394
[growls]

05:53.478 --> 05:54.854
[snarls]

06:00.401 --> 06:01.694
What's this for?

06:01.778 --> 06:03.154
Just hold on to them.

06:04.197 --> 06:05.531
If I don't make it back--

06:05.615 --> 06:06.866
Say no more.

06:09.535 --> 06:10.870
Then sell the pawnshop.

06:13.790 --> 06:15.041
Will you do that?

06:18.961 --> 06:21.756
[In-hyeok] The short fuses go off
after five minutes,

06:21.839 --> 06:24.092
and the long ones go off
after eight minutes.

06:24.884 --> 06:28.805
Each explosive has a blast radius
of about five or six meters.

06:28.888 --> 06:32.767
It may not bring the entire building down,
but it will do some major damage.

06:40.191 --> 06:41.359
Wait a second.

06:41.442 --> 06:42.860
Master Jang, wait.

06:45.029 --> 06:47.281
Good luck. I hope it all goes well.

06:47.365 --> 06:50.326
I will hold onto these
until you come back, okay?

06:51.577 --> 06:52.578
[chuckles softly]

06:59.001 --> 07:00.670
[Jun-taek] Sure you'll be fine
on your own?

07:00.753 --> 07:04.340
[Tae-sang] Yes, I know my way around,
so don't worry about me.

07:04.424 --> 07:05.967
It'd be better if I'm alone.

07:06.050 --> 07:08.803
I can get around much quicker.
Less chance of getting caught.

07:09.637 --> 07:10.555
Listen, Tae-sang--

07:10.638 --> 07:11.806
Wait till later.

07:13.141 --> 07:15.184
We can talk once this is finally over.

07:15.685 --> 07:17.812
How about we grab a drink
once we get through this?

07:19.647 --> 07:21.566
[chuckles] I look forward to it.

07:25.111 --> 07:26.112
[Tae-sang] Let's go.

07:42.044 --> 07:44.422
It appears
I have underestimated Lady Maeda.

07:44.505 --> 07:45.965
She's very resourceful.

07:46.048 --> 07:48.634
I wasn't sure
if we could find you in time,

07:48.718 --> 07:50.178
but she brought you right to me.

07:52.805 --> 07:53.806
You should know,

07:55.516 --> 07:57.810
your precious father
will be joining us very soon.

07:58.561 --> 08:01.063
This experiment will be
the first of its kind.

08:02.273 --> 08:03.483
A family reunion.

08:04.567 --> 08:06.402
I wonder who, between you two,

08:07.236 --> 08:08.988
will your mother devour first?

08:09.947 --> 08:13.117
I hope she goes for your father's head
just so you can watch.

08:13.201 --> 08:14.035
[seethes]

08:15.203 --> 08:17.580
[Chae-ok grunts, breathes heavily]

08:20.917 --> 08:23.503
[growling]

08:24.587 --> 08:25.922
[snarls]

08:28.925 --> 08:31.552
[roaring, growling]

08:34.180 --> 08:35.139
[distant snarling]

08:42.438 --> 08:44.524
Who goes there? Stop right there!

08:52.615 --> 08:54.242
[running footsteps receding]

08:58.246 --> 08:59.789
[tense music playing]

09:09.966 --> 09:11.092
So how is it

09:11.759 --> 09:12.927
that even now…

09:14.929 --> 09:16.847
you're not afraid of me whatsoever?

09:18.182 --> 09:20.184
You know that you can't win here.

09:21.185 --> 09:25.356
Yet still… you look at me
without any fear in your eyes.

09:26.357 --> 09:28.776
Since we're asking questions,
I have one for you.

09:31.237 --> 09:33.906
Why are you all so shameless
and proud of what you do in here?

09:36.534 --> 09:38.869
You completely violated my mother…

09:41.289 --> 09:43.833
and ruined my family
from having a happy life.

09:45.960 --> 09:50.006
You've murdered so many innocent people,
yet stand there so proud. It's delusional.

09:53.009 --> 09:55.928
How can you be so shameless
about everything you have done?

10:02.143 --> 10:05.479
The science I've done here
will create a new era in this world.

10:06.439 --> 10:08.441
This is my greatest achievement,

10:08.524 --> 10:10.985
and it towers
above your comprehension, Josenjing.

10:11.736 --> 10:12.612
[scoffs]

10:14.614 --> 10:15.781
[chuckles]

10:18.117 --> 10:19.827
You're no scientist.

10:22.955 --> 10:24.081
You're just crazy.

10:26.042 --> 10:29.086
Do you think by justifying
and glorifying what you did here…

10:31.339 --> 10:34.300
will erase all the crimes
you have committed here in Joseon?

10:36.093 --> 10:38.095
You can pretend all you want to,

10:38.179 --> 10:40.389
but it's crystal clear
to the rest of the world

10:40.473 --> 10:43.225
how inferior you must all feel
for you to occupy Joseon.

10:45.311 --> 10:46.771
[breathing heavily]

10:53.903 --> 10:55.863
- [dramatic music playing]
- [roaring]

10:55.946 --> 10:57.073
Lt. Kato?

11:01.786 --> 11:02.703
Lt. Kato!

11:03.537 --> 11:04.497
What is it now?!

11:05.373 --> 11:06.332
[soldiers scream]

11:07.333 --> 11:08.668
[screaming]

11:09.919 --> 11:11.545
- [booming]
- [clattering]

11:14.090 --> 11:15.299
[snarling]

11:16.050 --> 11:18.886
[roaring ferociously]

11:21.180 --> 11:22.473
[panicked screaming]

11:23.808 --> 11:24.975
[pained moaning]

11:39.240 --> 11:40.282
[snarling]

11:41.325 --> 11:42.493
[soldiers screaming]

11:46.497 --> 11:49.166
- [soldiers screaming]
- [creature snarling]

11:50.918 --> 11:52.294
[softly] Help me, Mother.

11:54.255 --> 11:55.297
[growls softly]

11:57.883 --> 11:59.385
[growling gently]

12:01.595 --> 12:03.055
[grunting]

12:05.558 --> 12:07.143
[creature howling]

12:07.727 --> 12:08.728
[Chae-ok gasping]

12:08.811 --> 12:10.563
[snarling]

12:12.356 --> 12:13.190
That's right.

12:14.316 --> 12:15.901
Don't move, or I'll shoot!

12:15.985 --> 12:17.486
Stay right where you are,

12:17.570 --> 12:19.780
or I will shoot her, Seishin.

12:21.157 --> 12:22.199
[roars]

12:24.660 --> 12:26.078
[rifles cocking]

12:26.162 --> 12:27.288
[Chae-ok gasping]

12:27.371 --> 12:28.706
[creature snarling]

12:30.458 --> 12:31.876
[roaring]

12:34.462 --> 12:35.463
Just do it!

12:36.005 --> 12:37.339
Shoot her now!

12:39.884 --> 12:41.051
[pained snarling]

12:41.135 --> 12:44.597
No!

12:44.680 --> 12:46.098
[solemn music playing]

12:46.182 --> 12:47.933
[snarling]

12:55.524 --> 12:56.609
[inaudible]

13:06.744 --> 13:10.080
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN THE END AND ANOTHER BEGINNING

13:10.164 --> 13:12.750
EPISODE 10

13:15.169 --> 13:16.212
[music fades]

13:17.421 --> 13:19.799
I heard that next month
you are returning to Tokyo.

13:21.342 --> 13:23.886
[sighs] Wow, I'm so jealous.

13:25.054 --> 13:27.723
Does that mean your anatomy book
will get published once you're there?

13:27.807 --> 13:28.682
It's a done deal?

13:30.392 --> 13:31.435
Yes, I suppose so.

13:32.186 --> 13:34.563
Whoa. Are you going to be famous?

13:39.443 --> 13:41.320
She's really pretty. Who is she?

13:42.571 --> 13:43.948
Your Josenjing girlfriend?

13:44.448 --> 13:47.201
No, it's Seishin.
It was when she first arrived.

13:48.244 --> 13:50.412
Wait, uh, seriously, that woman was her?

13:51.914 --> 13:52.873
Wow!

13:52.957 --> 13:55.000
She had such a pretty face.

13:55.084 --> 13:57.461
No wonder her husband
couldn't forget about her.

14:00.130 --> 14:01.298
Oh, she had a husband?

14:01.382 --> 14:04.468
What, you didn't know
that she had a husband and a daughter?

14:05.094 --> 14:06.053
Well, she did.

14:06.136 --> 14:08.639
And apparently,
her husband came looking for her.

14:08.722 --> 14:10.850
He requested that we let him see his wife.

14:23.404 --> 14:24.864
[tense music playing]

14:37.793 --> 14:41.213
MILITARY USE
GASOLINE

15:06.947 --> 15:09.658
- Master Jang, it's you.
- And it's you, sir.

15:11.535 --> 15:14.872
- [creature snarling in distance]
- [soldiers screaming in distance]

15:15.873 --> 15:17.625
Bring all the nitrogen gas we have!

15:17.708 --> 15:19.084
Release every canister!

15:19.168 --> 15:21.462
Do not let the creature
come up to this level!

15:21.545 --> 15:23.339
- [all] Yes, sir!
- [shushing]

15:26.258 --> 15:27.092
Be quiet.

15:33.140 --> 15:35.142
[creature snarling]

15:35.225 --> 15:37.102
It's the creature. Go get her!

15:38.187 --> 15:39.313
The rest of you,

15:40.773 --> 15:42.983
hold on to the woman. She goes with us.

15:43.067 --> 15:46.028
- [distant roaring]
- [dramatic music playing]

15:48.948 --> 15:50.824
So are you saying that my daughter

15:52.201 --> 15:54.870
was arrested and brought back
to this hospital again?

16:03.170 --> 16:04.296
Sir, I'm sorry.

16:05.255 --> 16:07.174
I should have never left
your daughter all alone.

16:15.808 --> 16:17.017
Here, take this.

16:19.228 --> 16:22.356
A ship is leaving to Shanghai
very early tomorrow morning.

16:23.232 --> 16:25.943
Chae-ok is wanted
for assassinating Director Ichiro.

16:26.485 --> 16:29.113
Your only way out of Joseon is
to board that ship with her.

16:31.073 --> 16:32.116
Listen, Master Jang.

16:32.199 --> 16:35.786
Whatever your plan was, I'll do it.
Just get yourself and Chae-ok out of here.

16:35.869 --> 16:38.080
She won't get onto that ship
unless you're with her.

16:52.594 --> 16:56.098
- [dramatic music playing]
- [creature roaring in distance]

16:58.350 --> 16:59.893
[snarling]

17:03.605 --> 17:04.523
[creature snarls]

17:04.606 --> 17:06.150
[Chae-ok breathing heavily]

17:06.775 --> 17:08.944
- [gas hissing]
- [creature roaring]

17:14.783 --> 17:15.743
Let her go!

17:16.368 --> 17:19.121
Don't let the creature pass through!
Soldiers, attack!

17:19.204 --> 17:20.330
Help me, Mother!

17:20.414 --> 17:21.540
[creature snarling]

17:21.623 --> 17:22.833
[gates closing]

17:23.667 --> 17:25.127
[Chae-ok grunting] No!

17:25.711 --> 17:27.796
- [gas hissing]
- [creature breathing heavily]

17:28.464 --> 17:30.549
[roaring furiously]

17:30.632 --> 17:32.009
[dramatic music continues]

17:34.219 --> 17:35.137
[soldier] Hurry!

17:43.103 --> 17:46.565
We have the creature blocked on level two.
I don't know how long we can hold it.

17:46.648 --> 17:48.067
Where is Lt. Kato?

17:48.150 --> 17:51.111
He was heading east towards
the emergency exit with the Joseon woman.

17:51.195 --> 17:53.989
Take your men to level two
and stop the creature from getting out.

17:54.073 --> 17:56.700
Do what you need to do to stop it.
Don't let it escape.

17:56.784 --> 17:57.618
Yes, sir!

17:59.119 --> 17:59.995
Damn it.

18:08.128 --> 18:10.380
That was Chae-ok they were talking about.

18:10.464 --> 18:13.217
I see an emergency stairwell
by the central elevator.

18:13.300 --> 18:16.053
We can get there undetected.
Let's head over that way.

18:18.597 --> 18:19.932
What are you doing? This is mine.

18:21.475 --> 18:23.143
Let me take care of this for you.

18:24.061 --> 18:26.855
I want you
to get Chae-ok out of here, understand?

18:28.065 --> 18:30.275
No, this is my responsibility.
Give it back.

18:30.359 --> 18:32.694
- Master Jang, I will do this.
- No, you won't!

18:32.778 --> 18:35.781
Not once have I ever placed
my responsibility onto somebody else.

18:35.864 --> 18:39.618
I'd never willingly put you or anyone
in this type of danger, so just forget it.

18:39.701 --> 18:42.121
Let me do this so I can keep you
and Chae-ok out of harms way.

18:42.204 --> 18:44.456
If you really want to protect my daughter,

18:45.290 --> 18:48.293
then the right thing to do
for her sake is to let me do this.

18:48.961 --> 18:49.878
When will you get it?

18:54.133 --> 18:55.134
Listen to me.

18:57.302 --> 18:59.680
This entire time,
I have been living in my past.

19:01.223 --> 19:04.101
And for once in the past ten years,
I… I see a future.

19:04.184 --> 19:05.477
A future for my daughter and you.

19:07.563 --> 19:11.066
My heart is full because I know
you will always have each other.

19:13.318 --> 19:15.028
I want to stay here with my wife.

19:16.155 --> 19:18.991
That is the job of a husband,
and I want to honor that.

19:27.499 --> 19:29.501
Master Jang, take care of Chae-ok.

19:31.837 --> 19:33.422
Please give her a happy life.

19:33.505 --> 19:35.090
[sentimental music playing]

19:36.633 --> 19:37.926
[breathing shakily]

19:38.802 --> 19:40.179
Promise me you'll do that.

19:47.352 --> 19:50.272
- [officer] Lt. Kato, sir!
- What's the situation?

19:50.355 --> 19:52.900
We are setting up a perimeter of defense
against the creature.

19:52.983 --> 19:54.318
Just in case, it might be best

19:54.401 --> 19:57.446
to shut down the underground laboratory
to prevent more casualties.

19:58.655 --> 20:00.991
I need to grab some things
from my lab first.

20:01.074 --> 20:02.326
Give me ten minutes.

20:03.410 --> 20:05.162
When I get back, close this entire level.

20:07.080 --> 20:09.791
- Take the woman to my upstairs office.
- Yes, sir!

20:14.755 --> 20:15.923
[yelling] Seishin!

20:17.883 --> 20:19.301
MILITARY USE
GASOLINE

20:19.384 --> 20:21.011
[dramatic music continues]

20:39.947 --> 20:42.115
[snarling ferociously]

20:42.866 --> 20:44.117
[roaring]

20:50.749 --> 20:51.917
[Chae-ok grunting]

20:53.335 --> 20:54.711
[soldiers yelling, grunting]

20:57.547 --> 21:00.384
You better stay still,
or I'll shoot you right here, understand?

21:01.134 --> 21:02.135
[gunshots]

21:15.190 --> 21:16.858
[dramatic music continues]

21:19.528 --> 21:20.654
[distant gunfire]

21:21.780 --> 21:22.990
[distant roaring]

21:23.073 --> 21:24.366
[distant screaming]

21:24.449 --> 21:26.034
[suspenseful music playing]

21:27.202 --> 21:29.079
[creature roaring]

21:29.162 --> 21:30.163
[glass shattering]

21:31.581 --> 21:32.457
[creature snarling]

21:39.172 --> 21:40.924
[growling menacingly]

21:43.343 --> 21:45.095
[snarling]

21:45.178 --> 21:46.388
[tense music playing]

22:07.159 --> 22:08.535
[creature snarling]

22:10.704 --> 22:11.913
No!

22:16.543 --> 22:17.377
[gasping]

22:18.295 --> 22:19.880
[creature roaring in distance]

22:22.007 --> 22:23.425
[breathing heavily]

22:24.509 --> 22:26.053
[Myeong-ja] Someone help me…

22:27.429 --> 22:28.597
My stomach,

22:30.057 --> 22:31.516
it hurts so much…

22:32.517 --> 22:34.895
[gasping] Someone please help.

22:37.481 --> 22:39.024
My baby…

22:40.067 --> 22:41.902
Please, somebody help.

22:43.153 --> 22:44.905
I don't wanna die.

22:47.032 --> 22:48.158
Help me, sir.

22:49.785 --> 22:53.705
[breathing heavily] My baby…
my baby is coming.

22:53.789 --> 22:55.040
[suspenseful music sting]

23:07.511 --> 23:09.346
[breathing heavily]

23:14.726 --> 23:16.645
[Chae-ok whimpering]

23:28.156 --> 23:29.199
Let's go this way.

23:31.827 --> 23:32.786
[bars clanging]

23:37.666 --> 23:42.337
[singing in Korean]
♪ I have heard no news ♪

23:42.421 --> 23:45.507
♪ Of the boat that left ♪

23:46.758 --> 23:51.513
♪ On the day of Chilseok ♪

23:52.681 --> 23:54.599
♪ Over there… ♪

23:54.683 --> 23:57.436
[growling softly]

23:57.519 --> 24:00.188
♪ …across the sea ♪

24:02.524 --> 24:05.026
[voice wavering] ♪ The boat returns… ♪

24:05.777 --> 24:06.736
[metal clanging]

24:09.614 --> 24:16.288
♪ And the song of the boatsman ♪

24:18.039 --> 24:22.711
♪ Draws nearer and nearer ♪

24:26.798 --> 24:30.635
♪ But you, my love ♪

24:30.719 --> 24:35.599
- ♪ I've not heard from you ♪
- [heavy footsteps approaching]

24:35.682 --> 24:40.520
♪ Ever since you left ♪

24:42.481 --> 24:43.857
[creature snarls curiously]

24:45.233 --> 24:47.402
[growling softly]

24:47.986 --> 24:49.571
[sentimental music playing]

24:53.033 --> 24:54.868
[growling in recognition]

25:03.084 --> 25:04.085
[creature snarls]

25:05.212 --> 25:06.213
[exhales forcefully]

25:06.296 --> 25:07.881
[creature growling softly]

25:11.301 --> 25:13.011
[snarling]

25:19.976 --> 25:21.478
Oh, sweetheart, there you are.

25:21.561 --> 25:22.979
[creature snarls]

25:23.772 --> 25:25.148
I've missed you so much.

25:27.651 --> 25:29.152
[growling gently]

25:30.779 --> 25:31.738
[breathing shakily]

25:34.366 --> 25:35.867
How about we leave together?

25:37.953 --> 25:40.455
Let's go and see our daughter.
How does that sound?

25:40.539 --> 25:42.457
[creature growling softly]

25:47.629 --> 25:49.548
[distant explosion]

26:16.825 --> 26:18.285
[boom echoing]

26:30.005 --> 26:31.006
[coughing]

26:32.173 --> 26:33.800
[both coughing]

26:51.693 --> 26:52.694
We better go.

26:55.447 --> 26:56.281
[grunts]

26:58.325 --> 27:00.535
We have to find a way out
while we still can.

27:01.369 --> 27:03.788
I can't!
Both of my parents are still down there.

27:05.790 --> 27:06.875
[Chae-ok sobbing]

27:08.501 --> 27:10.420
Listen to me.
It was your father's last request!

27:10.503 --> 27:11.588
[breathing heavily]

27:13.381 --> 27:16.551
I gave your father my word
that I would get you out of here safely.

27:18.219 --> 27:21.890
That is the promise I made to your father.
I intend to keep that promise.

27:25.393 --> 27:28.229
So you met my father,
and that's what he said to you?

27:28.813 --> 27:29.981
It's what he wanted.

27:31.483 --> 27:33.443
He wanted to be with your mother
one last time.

27:46.956 --> 27:47.832
[Chae-ok gasps]

27:51.711 --> 27:52.712
[sobbing]

27:53.755 --> 27:55.215
[solemn music playing]

28:03.682 --> 28:05.100
[sobbing]

28:24.452 --> 28:25.829
[sobbing continues]

29:19.632 --> 29:21.134
[solemn music continues]

29:25.388 --> 29:29.058
There was a large explosion
at Ongseong Hospital just now.

29:35.398 --> 29:38.485
Ongseong Hospital had a huge explosion
a couple of minutes ago!

29:39.068 --> 29:40.820
It shook the entire building!

29:40.904 --> 29:44.532
The fire department is on its way over,
but it's a complete disaster!

29:44.616 --> 29:45.992
[patrons gasping in shock]

29:46.785 --> 29:48.536
[distant sirens wailing]

29:50.288 --> 29:51.456
[music fades]

30:04.719 --> 30:06.221
[ominous music playing]

30:15.855 --> 30:17.690
[fireman 1] Hurry!
We have to put out this fire!

30:17.774 --> 30:20.443
- [fireman 2] Hurry! Let's go!
- [fireman 3] Put this out now!

30:20.527 --> 30:21.945
[fireman 1] Can't let it spread!

30:22.445 --> 30:24.614
[fireman 5] I need more water! More water!

30:24.697 --> 30:25.990
Bring more water!

30:26.074 --> 30:27.492
[fireman 2] Put it out, now!

30:34.374 --> 30:36.543
[soldier 1] The creature
is nowhere to be seen, sir.

30:36.626 --> 30:38.920
[soldier 2] It was not found
in Area One either.

30:39.420 --> 30:42.590
[soldier 3] What are the chances it died
in the fire or got crushed by the rubble?

30:42.674 --> 30:45.677
[soldier 1] There'd still be pieces of it.
There's nothing here.

30:45.760 --> 30:47.846
[solder 3] What?!
Where could it have gone?

30:47.929 --> 30:49.138
[soldier 1] I don't know, sir!

30:54.727 --> 30:56.145
[suspenseful music playing]

31:12.912 --> 31:14.706
[ominous music playing]

31:28.678 --> 31:29.929
[music fades]

31:45.445 --> 31:48.364
It looks like the entrance is open
thanks to all the firefighters.

31:49.157 --> 31:50.158
It's your way out.

31:50.700 --> 31:53.369
You can escape
through all the chaos that's happening.

31:55.455 --> 31:57.957
I got it from here.
You can't risk being seen with us.

31:59.167 --> 32:00.001
Master Jang…

32:00.084 --> 32:02.712
We appreciate all the help and support
you've given us, Sachimoto.

32:02.795 --> 32:04.297
We can't thank you enough.

32:05.006 --> 32:07.550
But I'm not letting you risk your life
helping us escape.

32:13.556 --> 32:15.683
Chae-ok, I want to apologize to you.

32:18.436 --> 32:19.646
I should have told you.

32:21.314 --> 32:24.400
I should have told you
I knew your mother and where she was.

32:26.569 --> 32:27.820
I am very sorry.

32:29.113 --> 32:32.241
I made excuses to myself
that there was nothing I could do

32:32.742 --> 32:34.535
because of the times we live in.

32:34.619 --> 32:35.620
But the truth is,

32:36.788 --> 32:37.830
I was afraid.

32:39.624 --> 32:40.875
I should have helped her.

32:43.628 --> 32:45.129
Instead, I was just a bystander.

32:47.632 --> 32:48.716
We understand.

32:51.344 --> 32:53.930
Sachimoto, please take care of yourself.

33:20.873 --> 33:22.375
[sobbing quietly]

33:30.591 --> 33:31.968
[dramatic music playing]

33:34.887 --> 33:36.305
[creature growling softly]

33:43.980 --> 33:45.440
[tires screeching]

33:46.024 --> 33:49.360
- [fireman 1] We need more help!
- [fireman 2] Help us put this fire out!

33:49.861 --> 33:50.945
[yelling]

33:52.947 --> 33:55.408
[fireman 3] We need
to get this thing under control now!

34:23.352 --> 34:24.520
[panting]

34:27.148 --> 34:29.067
[guttural growling]

34:30.276 --> 34:31.986
[solemn music playing]

34:51.297 --> 34:52.548
[music fades]

35:40.847 --> 35:42.140
[knocking on door]

35:42.223 --> 35:43.850
[Mrs. Nawol breathes shakily]

35:45.601 --> 35:46.435
Oh.

35:47.728 --> 35:48.646
Newspaper, ma'am.

35:48.729 --> 35:50.815
I'm here on behalf of Mr. Wang tonight.

35:50.898 --> 35:52.567
He said this was a message
from Master Jang.

35:57.864 --> 35:59.907
[breathing heavily]

36:27.685 --> 36:31.063
Beom-o, listen, get Mr. Park over here.
Tell him it's very urgent.

36:31.147 --> 36:32.648
Tell him to bring his rickshaw. Go!

36:32.732 --> 36:35.902
Hold on there… Huh? I will do it.
Taking a car would be a lot faster.

36:35.985 --> 36:38.029
And what if the police bureau sees you?

36:38.112 --> 36:39.989
Nobody will notice me.
I'll be very careful!

36:40.072 --> 36:42.617
Just stop it.
We have to be very discreet here.

36:42.700 --> 36:43.659
[Mr. Gu sighs]

36:43.743 --> 36:46.204
Let me do it. I can deliver it for you.

36:47.330 --> 36:50.333
If I use my bicycle, I can get there
a lot quicker than a rickshaw.

36:50.416 --> 36:53.628
The police won't notice
because they never pay attention to me.

36:57.215 --> 36:58.507
Just give me a chance.

37:00.092 --> 37:02.720
I want the opportunity
to prove that I'm trustworthy.

37:03.429 --> 37:04.305
Please?

37:20.655 --> 37:22.198
[ominous music playing]

37:26.077 --> 37:27.245
[Maeda's butler] Follow him.

37:34.043 --> 37:34.877
Thank you, Mr. Wang.

37:34.961 --> 37:37.964
In the morning, please visit Mrs. Nawol
to receive your final payment.

37:38.047 --> 37:40.549
Please be careful, Master Jang.

37:51.644 --> 37:54.438
VICIOUS KILLER

38:13.958 --> 38:16.961
I arranged passage for us
to Incheon. We better go.

38:28.389 --> 38:29.307
What's the matter?

38:32.518 --> 38:34.312
Why don't we end things here?

38:40.026 --> 38:41.944
From this point forward, I go on alone.

38:43.195 --> 38:44.447
What do you mean, go on alone?

38:44.530 --> 38:47.158
I'm the one
who killed Director Ichiro, not you.

38:48.659 --> 38:50.411
It's me they are looking for here.

38:50.995 --> 38:54.081
I may have to live the rest of my life
constantly on the run,

38:54.165 --> 38:57.793
never knowing when I'll be killed
or if I will get to live another day.

38:57.877 --> 39:00.129
And I've made the decision
to go with you anyway.

39:00.212 --> 39:02.840
It just doesn't make sense
to drag you into this.

39:05.426 --> 39:07.845
It's not fair for you
to carry my burden as well.

39:12.600 --> 39:14.852
[tender music playing]

39:20.066 --> 39:21.359
Do you not, um…

39:26.322 --> 39:27.239
like me?

39:29.784 --> 39:31.702
That's not what I was trying to say.

39:32.203 --> 39:35.164
[chuckles softly]
For a second there, I was a bit worried.

39:37.458 --> 39:39.043
We're sticking together, no matter what.

39:39.126 --> 39:40.961
Are you sure about this?

39:41.045 --> 39:41.962
I am.

39:45.007 --> 39:47.760
Remember… when you were looking for me?

39:50.221 --> 39:52.139
This man standing in front of you now

39:53.307 --> 39:55.643
barely escaped death
the first time around.

39:57.228 --> 39:58.896
I'm here all because…

40:01.190 --> 40:03.275
I've been given a second chance.

40:04.777 --> 40:06.278
So this time I'm staying by your side.

40:08.614 --> 40:10.950
They'll never stop looking for us.
You know that, right?

40:11.033 --> 40:13.077
I'll do whatever's needed to protect us.

40:17.415 --> 40:19.667
I can't imagine my life
without you, Chae-ok.

40:20.668 --> 40:22.044
We're meant for each other.

41:03.711 --> 41:04.879
It found a way out.

41:05.463 --> 41:07.006
[unsettling music playing]

41:22.855 --> 41:25.191
[distant roaring]

41:25.274 --> 41:26.817
[brakes squeaking]

41:26.901 --> 41:28.694
[heavy footsteps stomping]

41:28.777 --> 41:29.820
[snarling]

41:52.134 --> 41:53.135
[Tae-sang sighs]

41:55.804 --> 41:57.640
[unsettling music playing]

42:04.146 --> 42:05.898
[music intensifies]

42:48.148 --> 42:49.275
[engine starts]

42:52.152 --> 42:53.404
[music fades]

42:53.487 --> 42:54.613
[sighs]

42:55.364 --> 42:57.116
We can't delay our escape any longer.

42:57.199 --> 42:59.201
We have to make our way to Incheon
or be left behind.

43:00.327 --> 43:01.870
[distant gravel crunching]

43:07.501 --> 43:09.044
Someone's coming, look.

43:10.504 --> 43:11.839
[Beom-o breathing heavily]

43:15.175 --> 43:16.343
[Beom-o grunts]

43:18.762 --> 43:20.723
- Beom-o! Are you okay?
- Yes.

43:21.765 --> 43:22.891
I'm sorry I'm so late.

43:22.975 --> 43:25.394
I had to shake someone off my tail
along the way.

43:29.148 --> 43:30.274
[vehicle approaching]

43:30.899 --> 43:32.151
[ominous music playing]

43:36.488 --> 43:37.865
[tires screeching]

43:43.412 --> 43:44.455
[tires squealing]

44:21.116 --> 44:23.619
Well done, Shiro. You did good.

44:25.454 --> 44:27.915
I didn't do anything.
It's not what it looks like.

44:27.998 --> 44:31.669
I didn't mean for this to happen.
I swear to you, Master Jang. I swear.

44:36.423 --> 44:38.967
Get outta here.
Find somewhere safe to hide.

44:46.934 --> 44:47.935
In any case,

44:49.186 --> 44:51.188
it seems you are a man of your word.

44:52.439 --> 44:54.274
Once you set your mind on something,

44:54.358 --> 44:57.069
you go through great lengths
to make sure you succeed.

44:58.278 --> 45:00.406
Although demolishing an entire hospital

45:01.365 --> 45:02.700
was a bit excessive, no?

45:03.617 --> 45:07.246
Yet it doesn't compare to what you all did
to those people imprisoned there.

45:07.913 --> 45:10.499
Oh really, now? What are you going to do?

45:12.418 --> 45:14.670
Will you really give up everything

45:14.753 --> 45:15.838
for that rebel woman?

45:15.921 --> 45:17.923
A poor Josenjing, no less.

45:18.006 --> 45:20.467
I already gave you my answer.
It hasn't changed.

45:26.181 --> 45:27.099
[chuckles wryly]

45:32.813 --> 45:35.858
There was once a time
I considered you a true friend.

45:35.941 --> 45:38.944
To be honest, I never thought
this is how it would end for us.

45:39.445 --> 45:42.114
But I suppose our friendship
wasn't meant to last anyway.

45:46.034 --> 45:47.119
Come to think of it,

45:47.703 --> 45:49.204
why, this is quite familiar.

45:49.830 --> 45:52.458
Unfortunately, you are not
the only friend to have turned against me.

45:54.960 --> 45:57.045
There's a woman from my childhood.

45:59.506 --> 46:01.592
To think your mother and I
were once friends.

46:06.930 --> 46:08.015
[sighs]

46:14.480 --> 46:15.522
It seems

46:16.523 --> 46:18.150
the two of you will have to die.

46:18.650 --> 46:20.277
This is the end for both of you.

46:24.740 --> 46:25.699
So long.

46:32.372 --> 46:33.665
[music fades]

46:39.755 --> 46:41.089
[tense music playing]

46:46.595 --> 46:48.472
[music building]

47:05.239 --> 47:06.114
Attack!

47:06.198 --> 47:07.157
[men yelling]

47:14.164 --> 47:15.082
[gunshot]

47:18.627 --> 47:19.628
- [gunshot]
- [groans]

47:28.846 --> 47:29.972
[gunshot]

47:41.441 --> 47:42.359
[pained groaning]

47:45.320 --> 47:46.238
[pained grunt]

47:48.657 --> 47:49.658
[yelling]

47:52.786 --> 47:54.872
- [ominous music playing]
- [pained groaning]

47:57.624 --> 47:58.625
[pained grunt]

48:12.848 --> 48:13.891
[creature growls]

48:15.517 --> 48:16.810
[roaring]

48:18.812 --> 48:20.522
- [knife slicing]
- [pained groaning]

48:29.448 --> 48:30.741
[straining]

48:36.371 --> 48:37.956
[dramatic music playing]

48:38.498 --> 48:40.125
[creature roaring]

49:02.940 --> 49:03.857
[pained grunt]

49:36.723 --> 49:38.308
[both breathing heavily]

49:50.570 --> 49:52.406
[panting]

49:56.284 --> 49:57.369
[men yelling]

50:00.706 --> 50:02.124
[dramatic music playing]

50:03.166 --> 50:05.752
[growling, snarling]

50:12.676 --> 50:14.469
[roaring]

50:17.389 --> 50:18.390
[men yelling]

50:23.687 --> 50:24.813
[creature roaring]

50:27.607 --> 50:28.775
[creature snarling]

50:29.401 --> 50:31.403
[roaring ferociously]

50:38.618 --> 50:39.703
[Tae-sang] We have to go.

50:40.203 --> 50:41.830
[Chae-ok grunting weakly]

50:43.040 --> 50:44.416
[growling softly]

50:48.295 --> 50:49.713
[men yelling]

50:53.508 --> 50:54.843
[creature screeching]

50:54.926 --> 50:56.470
[roaring]

51:01.725 --> 51:03.435
[pained screeching]

51:05.896 --> 51:08.690
[roaring]

51:14.696 --> 51:16.239
[screeching]

51:28.085 --> 51:29.544
[music fades]

51:34.674 --> 51:35.759
[growling]

51:37.719 --> 51:38.637
Hang on to me! [grunts]

51:40.097 --> 51:41.848
[growling]

51:41.932 --> 51:42.808
Chae-ok.

51:43.517 --> 51:44.392
Get up.

51:45.519 --> 51:47.479
- Chae-ok.
- [creature growling]

51:48.313 --> 51:49.689
[growling]

51:49.773 --> 51:50.857
[footsteps thundering]

51:54.778 --> 51:55.946
Get up, Chae-ok.

51:59.741 --> 52:00.742
[snarling]

52:02.285 --> 52:03.411
[flesh squelching]

52:03.495 --> 52:04.538
[silence]

52:21.138 --> 52:22.931
Mother, please. [spluttering]

52:24.141 --> 52:25.392
[breathing shakily]

52:26.017 --> 52:29.020
You… have to stop this…

52:29.104 --> 52:31.356
[growling softly]

52:31.857 --> 52:33.608
[labored breathing]

52:34.651 --> 52:38.613
I know you're… you're in pain.
I understand. [splutters]

52:40.615 --> 52:42.450
[groaning]

52:43.618 --> 52:44.494
[Chae-ok] I…

52:46.079 --> 52:47.080
[pained grunting]

52:50.250 --> 52:51.585
I love him.

52:53.920 --> 52:54.921
[sobbing]

52:56.256 --> 53:00.302
He is someone
that I love so much, like you.

53:01.136 --> 53:02.053
[sobbing]

53:02.137 --> 53:04.222
- [tender music playing]
- [Chae-ok] Mother!

53:06.933 --> 53:08.059
Please…

53:09.769 --> 53:12.439
let's… let's just stop this, okay?

53:16.234 --> 53:17.611
[moaning]

53:20.655 --> 53:22.324
Let's just stop this, huh?

53:27.787 --> 53:29.831
[creature groaning]

53:32.709 --> 53:33.668
[Tae-sang] Chae-ok.

53:35.170 --> 53:36.588
- Chae-ok… Chae-ok!
- [spluttering]

53:40.759 --> 53:41.593
Chae-ok!

53:42.928 --> 53:45.805
You're gonna be okay.
Just hold on a little longer.

53:47.474 --> 53:48.683
[panicked muttering]

53:48.767 --> 53:50.602
We said that we'd be together.

53:53.104 --> 53:55.065
Just try… to hang on to me.

53:55.565 --> 53:57.817
Chae-ok, please… just try to get up.

54:04.491 --> 54:06.117
[breathing shakily]

54:06.826 --> 54:08.828
Master Jang, look, the cherry…

54:13.333 --> 54:15.543
blossoms have lost their flowers.

54:16.044 --> 54:17.295
[solemn music playing]

54:48.535 --> 54:49.828
[Tae-sang] Stay with me, Chae-ok.

54:52.872 --> 54:53.957
Stay by my side.

54:56.293 --> 54:57.794
I want you to stay with me.

54:58.295 --> 55:04.009
["Time" by Baek A playing]
♪ Will it come when winter's gone? ♪

55:04.092 --> 55:04.926
[sobbing]

55:05.010 --> 55:09.389
♪ Will it come when spring… ♪

55:09.472 --> 55:10.390
Chae-ok.

55:11.558 --> 55:12.392
No!

55:12.475 --> 55:16.146
- ♪ Before the cherry blossoms fall ♪
- [Tae-sang] Don't leave me, please!

55:16.229 --> 55:18.440
Please! No! Why?!

55:18.523 --> 55:20.233
Why?! [sobbing uncontrollably]

55:23.028 --> 55:25.989
No! Why?!

55:26.072 --> 55:27.449
[wailing sobs]

55:29.576 --> 55:30.952
Please don't leave me!

55:37.375 --> 55:39.461
[growling]

55:39.544 --> 55:41.004
[Tae-sang] Please don't go!

55:42.255 --> 55:44.007
- [sobbing]
- [Tae-sang crying]

55:45.508 --> 55:47.010
[sobbing uncontrollably]

55:50.597 --> 55:54.225
Oh, please, come back.
I… I'm begging you. Please!

55:56.770 --> 55:58.146
[solemn music playing]

56:09.157 --> 56:11.034
[creature groaning]

56:19.000 --> 56:21.544
[creature roaring]

56:24.297 --> 56:25.465
[music fades]

56:52.075 --> 56:53.410
[soldier] Lt. Kato!

56:53.493 --> 56:54.702
Lt. Kato!

57:13.346 --> 57:14.431
Lt. Kato!

57:26.443 --> 57:27.277
[gasps]

57:29.946 --> 57:31.739
- Lt. Kato!
- [Kato] Shh!

57:36.202 --> 57:37.203
Don't wake it up.

57:52.302 --> 57:53.178
[chuckles]

57:56.264 --> 57:57.140
[sniffles]

58:04.939 --> 58:06.107
It's beautiful.

58:07.150 --> 58:08.401
[slithering]

58:18.912 --> 58:20.079
[solemn music playing]

58:38.139 --> 58:41.226
My friend asked that I personally
deliver this message to you.

58:44.729 --> 58:45.813
What friend?

58:47.148 --> 58:50.026
His name is… Master Jang.
I believe you've met.

59:19.389 --> 59:21.891
FAREWELL

59:27.021 --> 59:28.690
[tense music playing]

59:54.632 --> 59:57.218
FROM JUNG TAE-SANG
OF THE HOUSE OF GOLDEN TREASURE

59:58.678 --> 01:00:01.848
FROM AKIKO
COURTESAN OF SPRING MOON HALL

01:00:01.931 --> 01:00:04.434
FROM PRIVATE CHOI YEONG-GWAN
OF DISEASE CONTROL PLATOON

01:00:06.811 --> 01:00:08.146
FROM YOON JUNG-WON
SLEUTH

01:00:08.229 --> 01:00:11.232
FROM YOON CHAE-OK
SLEUTH

01:00:14.861 --> 01:00:17.363
FROM CHOI SEONG-SIM

01:00:17.447 --> 01:00:18.865
[music building]

01:00:24.120 --> 01:00:25.538
[breathing shakily]

01:00:35.757 --> 01:00:38.718
FAREWELL

01:00:40.720 --> 01:00:41.804
[gasps]

01:00:50.980 --> 01:00:52.523
[explosion echoing]

01:00:54.692 --> 01:00:57.111
[woman 1] It's so beautiful tonight.

01:00:57.195 --> 01:00:58.946
[woman 2] I know! Drinks are on me.

01:00:59.030 --> 01:01:00.198
[indistinct chattering]

01:01:01.074 --> 01:01:02.450
[Jun-taek] In the end,

01:01:02.533 --> 01:01:04.035
justice will prevail.

01:01:05.119 --> 01:01:06.537
We are finally free now.

01:01:06.621 --> 01:01:08.998
[classical piano music
playing in background]

01:01:13.336 --> 01:01:15.463
And in the end,
you were a tremendous help.

01:01:16.464 --> 01:01:19.842
If you hadn't come with me that day
to convince Comrade Lee In-Hyeok,

01:01:19.926 --> 01:01:22.011
this rebellion
would not have been successful.

01:01:22.095 --> 01:01:25.556
[clicks tongue] So it turns out
you're a patriot after all.

01:01:44.033 --> 01:01:45.201
Thanks for the drink.

01:01:45.952 --> 01:01:47.078
I'll see you later.

01:01:48.788 --> 01:01:50.081
Oh! Comrade Jang!

01:01:54.585 --> 01:01:57.463
What a big achievement it is
to fight for our nation's freedom.

01:01:57.547 --> 01:02:01.592
We heard everything you did.
You're a fighter. You're a true patriot.

01:02:01.676 --> 01:02:02.760
- Huh?
- Hear, hear!

01:02:02.844 --> 01:02:03.803
That's right!

01:02:08.349 --> 01:02:10.685
By any chance,
are you in desperate need for money?

01:02:11.602 --> 01:02:12.437
What's that?

01:02:12.520 --> 01:02:14.731
If you have
any valuable items to pawn off,

01:02:14.814 --> 01:02:16.190
swing by my shop.

01:02:16.274 --> 01:02:17.859
I'll make sure you get a good deal.

01:02:20.737 --> 01:02:22.155
Oh, by the way,

01:02:22.238 --> 01:02:24.532
don't ever call me Comrade Jang again.

01:02:24.615 --> 01:02:27.410
I'm Master Jang
of the House of Golden Treasure.

01:02:28.035 --> 01:02:28.870
Well, then.

01:02:31.205 --> 01:02:32.165
[door opens]

01:02:33.249 --> 01:02:34.625
[chuckling]

01:02:35.376 --> 01:02:36.335
[door closes]

01:02:40.089 --> 01:02:41.382
[Jun-taek] Listen, Tae-sang.

01:02:42.592 --> 01:02:44.677
I need to be really honest with you here.

01:02:46.095 --> 01:02:47.972
I betrayed you and gave up your name.

01:02:49.182 --> 01:02:50.725
I ratted out my best friend.

01:02:51.267 --> 01:02:53.102
Actually, I ratted out everybody.

01:02:54.228 --> 01:02:56.606
I was tortured
and begged for my life like a coward.

01:02:58.149 --> 01:02:58.983
[chuckles]

01:03:01.861 --> 01:03:03.905
We can talk once this is finally over.

01:03:04.405 --> 01:03:06.783
How about we grab a drink
once we get through this?

01:03:18.795 --> 01:03:21.506
[silk vendor] Silk!
Come take a look at our silk!

01:03:21.589 --> 01:03:23.216
[indistinct chattering]

01:03:25.676 --> 01:03:26.803
[man 1] Have a taste.

01:03:26.886 --> 01:03:29.597
[man 2] Oh, thank you. This is delicious.

01:03:32.809 --> 01:03:33.684
[silk vendor] Silk!

01:03:34.644 --> 01:03:36.938
- [woman 1] Yes.
- [man 3] Special sale tonight.

01:03:37.563 --> 01:03:38.940
[woman 2] Good evening, sir.

01:03:39.023 --> 01:03:41.192
[man 4] Ask them
to bring some green onion.

01:03:41.275 --> 01:03:43.945
- [woman 3] Absolutely.
- [man 5] Please slice some of that meat.

01:03:44.028 --> 01:03:46.572
- Yes, that's good.
- [man 6] Hey, excuse me!

01:03:46.656 --> 01:03:47.907
I'd like one gukbap!

01:03:48.741 --> 01:03:51.285
- [heartwarming music playing]
- [man 7] Please move out of the way.

01:03:51.369 --> 01:03:52.662
Sorry, I need the space.

01:03:54.038 --> 01:03:55.706
[man 8] I'll take two of those.

01:04:01.796 --> 01:04:04.131
How about we go inside?
The night's getting cold.

01:04:21.023 --> 01:04:22.608
[motorcycle passing nearby]

01:04:24.694 --> 01:04:27.822
[instrumental version
of "Time" by Baek A playing]

01:04:44.088 --> 01:04:45.172
[Tae-sang] That year,

01:04:45.256 --> 01:04:48.843
that particular spring in Gyeongseong
passed by in the blink of an eye.

01:05:53.491 --> 01:05:55.284
And in August of that year,

01:05:57.244 --> 01:06:00.790
we finally recovered
what was taken from us.

01:06:02.249 --> 01:06:04.085
[stifles sob]

01:06:08.297 --> 01:06:09.548
As she once said,

01:06:11.217 --> 01:06:12.635
the cherry blossoms

01:06:13.719 --> 01:06:15.596
have already begun to fall.

01:06:16.138 --> 01:06:17.056
[chuckles sadly]

01:06:19.934 --> 01:06:21.852
[sighs, sniffles]

01:06:30.069 --> 01:06:31.487
[music fades]

01:06:35.992 --> 01:06:38.452
[man on radio] The welfare of the wounded
and the war sufferers

01:06:38.536 --> 01:06:40.538
and those who have lost
their homes and livelihoods

01:06:40.621 --> 01:06:42.748
are the objects
of our profound solicitude.

01:06:42.832 --> 01:06:45.626
[crowd] Hooray
for the independence of Korea!

01:06:45.710 --> 01:06:48.587
[man] Hooray
for the independence of Korea!

01:06:48.671 --> 01:06:51.173
[crowd] Hooray
for the independence of Korea!

01:06:51.257 --> 01:06:52.341
[door opens]

01:06:52.425 --> 01:06:53.634
[footsteps approaching]

01:06:54.260 --> 01:06:55.094
[door closes]

01:06:55.177 --> 01:06:56.387
[footsteps approaching]

01:07:04.437 --> 01:07:05.563
Lady Maeda.

01:07:12.111 --> 01:07:15.531
As of today, Ongseong Hospital
is closing its doors permanently.

01:07:15.614 --> 01:07:16.490
[liquid pouring]

01:07:20.494 --> 01:07:22.496
The entire staff will be leaving.

01:07:23.164 --> 01:07:25.499
They will return to Japan
within a fortnight.

01:07:28.961 --> 01:07:31.172
You must also make a decision.

01:07:34.175 --> 01:07:37.386
Now that you no longer have
a purpose in Gyeongseong,

01:07:37.470 --> 01:07:38.971
will you go back to Kyoto?

01:07:39.472 --> 01:07:40.306
Or…

01:07:41.974 --> 01:07:45.603
would you like to continue exploring
new possibilities together with me?

01:08:07.750 --> 01:08:08.626
[door opens]

01:08:12.505 --> 01:08:13.339
[door closes]

01:08:14.090 --> 01:08:15.424
[footsteps receding]

01:08:43.577 --> 01:08:44.703
[Tae-sang] As for me,

01:08:45.454 --> 01:08:48.624
I'm still waiting
for what I have dreamed of.

01:08:49.834 --> 01:08:52.878
["Time (Elec. ver.)" by LEAFY playing]

